`Noisy` prints its name when dropped:

```rust
struct Noisy(&'static str);

impl Drop for Noisy {
    fn drop(&mut self) {
        println!("{}", self.0);
    }
}

fn main() {
    let _a = Noisy("a");
    let b = Noisy("b");
    {
        let _c = Noisy("c");
        drop(b);
    }
    println!("end");
}
```

What does it print? Write the four lines separated by spaces.

